<title>FRANCE: France's SNCF sees 1997 loss of two bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>France's SNCF sees 1997 loss of two bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The SNCF railways expects to incur a loss of two billion francs ($351.6 million) in 1997 following a government plan to spin off 134.2 billion francs of the company's debt, financial daily Les Echos reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Les Echos, citing chairman Louis Gallois, said the loss for 1997 would have reached 15 billion francs if the government had not agreed the SNCF reform. Parliament approved the plan last Friday.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452 ($ = 5.688 French Francs)</p>
